    <dashboard name='Notes'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/LogisticsDashboardv4/Notes?rev=' id='Notes' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/LogisticsDashboardv4' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='58458' id='3' type-v2='text' w='99318' x='341' y='6410'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='15'>Notes on the use of the dashboard</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>The  logistics dashboard has the purpose of showing the main logistics KPIs on a daily, weekly and monthly level.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>The dashboard has several filters which let the user dig in the desired granularity of data. The metrics comes from the 3 sources, namely </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>hurrier orders</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>, </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>rooster</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>, and </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>hurrier rider transitions</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Some of the KPIs are not connected across the 3 aforementioned sources, thus </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>not</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'> all the shown metrics are computable for the all single levels of granularity. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Below a few examples with more details: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Entity Display Name</run>
              <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: The display name is used by logistics to show the venture and the country. Some countries have more than one entity, all separated, while other countries even having more than one entity they are in the same environment (Eg: Sweden, Finland, Canada, Saudi Arabia). For  the latter cases rooster data is not separable, therefore, you will see hours at a country, city, zone, contract, vehicle level but not based on Entity.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Is preorder</run>
              <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: As this tag is related to the orders, this information comes exclusively from Hurrier. Therefore, you won&apos;t be able to display Rooster data if you select true or false, and thus UTR displayed won&apos;t be per tag. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Vehicle/Bag</run>
              <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: This is the combination of vehicle name + bag that rider used to complete the order, this filter is relevant only for completed orders. Moreover, the filter applies to rooster data with the rule of vehicle with most orders during the granularity choosen (day, week, month). </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Zone Name</run>
              <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: This is the dropoff zone of the order and it&apos;s available for both completed and cancelled orders. Please bear in mind that some orders (even if rare case) might end up in zones not covered in hurrier. For rooster data this is the zone corresponding to the starting point the shift is assigned.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Contract Name and Type</run>
              <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: This filter is relevant for completed orders and for cancelled orders that had a rider assigned. For orders cancelled before a rider is assigned, filter is not relevant.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Vertical Type</run>
              <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: As this tag is related to the orders, this information comes exclusively from Hurrier. Therefore, you won&apos;t be able to display Rooster data if you select one of the verticals, and thus UTR displayed won&apos;t be per tag. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='5796' id='60' is-centered='0' is-scaled='1' param='Image/DH logo standard.PNG' type-v2='bitmap' w='99318' x='341' y='614'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='34518' id='61' type-v2='empty' w='99318' x='341' y='64868'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='58' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='98044' id='59' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99004' x='498' y='978'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='92373' id='3' type-v2='text' w='99004' x='498' y='6649'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='15'>Notes on the use of the dashboard</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>The  logistics dashboard has the purpose of showing the main logistics KPIs on a daily, weekly and monthly level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>The dashboard has several filters which let the user dig in the desired granularity of data. The metrics comes from the 3 sources, namely </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>hurrier orders</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>, </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>rooster</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>, and </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>hurrier rider transitions</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Some of the KPIs are not connected across the 3 aforementioned sources, thus </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>not</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'> all the shown metrics are computable for the all single levels of granularity. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Below a few examples with more details: </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Entity Display Name</run>
                    <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: The display name is used by logistics to show the venture and the country. Some countries have more than one entity, all separated, while other countries even having more than one entity they are in the same environment (Eg: Sweden, Finland, Canada, Saudi Arabia). For  the latter cases rooster data is not separable, therefore, you will see hours at a country, city, zone, contract, vehicle level but not based on Entity.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Is preorder</run>
                    <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: As this tag is related to the orders, this information comes exclusively from Hurrier. Therefore, you won&apos;t be able to display Rooster data if you select true or false, and thus UTR displayed won&apos;t be per tag. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Vehicle/Bag</run>
                    <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: This is the combination of vehicle name + bag that rider used to complete the order, this filter is relevant only for completed orders. Moreover, the filter applies to rooster data with the rule of vehicle with most orders during the granularity choosen (day, week, month). </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Zone Name</run>
                    <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: This is the dropoff zone of the order and it&apos;s available for both completed and cancelled orders. Please bear in mind that some orders (even if rare case) might end up in zones not covered in hurrier. For rooster data this is the zone corresponding to the starting point the shift is assigned.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Contract Name and Type</run>
                    <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: This filter is relevant for completed orders and for cancelled orders that had a rider assigned. For orders cancelled before a rider is assigned, filter is not relevant.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>☞  Vertical Type</run>
                    <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>: As this tag is related to the orders, this information comes exclusively from Hurrier. Therefore, you won&apos;t be able to display Rooster data if you select one of the verticals, and thus UTR displayed won&apos;t be per tag. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
